Tatoeba
  https://tatoeba.org
  Sentences licensed under CC BY 2.0 FR
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/).

  tools/corpus.tsv holds sentences from the Tatoeba per-language exports,
  each row with the Tatoeba ids of its sentences; tools/gen_corpus.py
  describes how they were chosen and the changes made to some rows
  (Romanian cedillas, Vietnamese tone marks for windows-1258, Hebrew in
  reverse order, simplified Chinese chosen as text Big5 cannot represent).
  golden_data_test.mbt contains these sentences encoded in UTF-8, the CJK
  encodings and single-byte encodings, and decode_data_test.mbt prefixes of
  some of them encoded in the encodings of the Encoding Standard, with their
  text. README.mbt.md, cmd/main/main_wbtest.mbt, demo/demo_test.mbt and
  tools/check_demo.mjs quote some of them with their ids; demo/app.js holds
  four of them, encoded, as samples, and demo/index.html lists their ids.
  bench_test.mbt repeats those of golden_data_test.mbt as the inputs of the
  benchmarks.

Tools
  tools/golden builds against the crates chardetng 1.0.0 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT)
  and encoding_rs 0.8.42 ((Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause), with the
  versions of their dependencies pinned in tools/golden/Cargo.lock.
  tools/sniffer runs the npm packages html-encoding-sniffer 7.0.0 (MIT,
  Copyright © Domenic Denicola) and @exodus/bytes 1.16.0 (MIT, Copyright (c)
  2024-2025 Exodus Movement), pinned in tools/sniffer/package-lock.json; to
  follow the HTML Standard where html-encoding-sniffer departs from it,
  tools/sniffer/main.mjs edits four of its lines in memory, which it quotes.
  tools/gen_xml_data.py runs expat (MIT License, Copyright (c) 1998-2000
  Thai Open Source Software Center Ltd and Clark Cooper, Copyright (c)
  2001-2025 Expat maintainers) through the pyexpat module of Python;
  xml_data_test.mbt holds answers that follow from what it reads.
  These packages are used to produce test data and are not part of the
  MoonBit module.
